  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elevated Technologies Services obligated $78M in FY2027 to date. Elevated Technologies Services received 24 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $3.3M. Obligations fell 74.9% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, obligating $75.5M of the company’s FY2027 to-date total. Other federal buyers with obligations include the General Services Administration with $2.5M and the Department of Justice with $7.2K. Elevated Technologies Services’ work is concentrated in a few NAICS markets. Other Building Equipment Contractors accounts for $73.2M of obligations, followed by Facilities Support Services at $4.2M and Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment (except Automotive and Electronic) Repair and Maintenance at $659K. Historical obligations show growth and contraction across recent fiscal years: FY22 was $36.4M, FY23 was $67.9M, FY24 was $51.1M, FY25 was $68.3M, and FY26 was $311M. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date), and award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than current-year obligations.",
